  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0423' contains 7 tables. The tables are described as follows:\n1. **Course**: This table holds information about the courses. The primary key is 'Course_ID', which is an integer. The columns include 'Course_category', 'Course_description', 'Course_name', 'Difficulty_level', 'Number_of_lessons', 'Recommended', 'Target_audience', and 'Total_duration'. All these columns allow null values.\n2. **Chapter**: This table holds information about the chapters of the courses. The primary key is 'Chapter_ID', which is an integer. The columns include 'Chapter_description', 'Chapter_name', 'Duration', 'Next_chapter_ID', 'Parent_chapter_ID', 'Previous_chapter_ID', 'Video_URL'. The 'Next_chapter_ID', 'Parent_chapter_ID', and 'Previous_chapter_ID' columns all reference the 'Chapter_ID' in the 'Chapter' table.\n3. **Instructor**: This table holds information about the instructors. The primary key is 'Instructor_ID', which is an integer. The columns include 'Avatar', 'Name', 'Personal_profile', 'Professional_field', and 'Teaching_experience'. All these columns allow null values.\n4. **Student**: This table holds information about the students. The primary key is 'Student_ID', which is an integer. The columns include 'Account_status', 'Age', 'Avatar', 'Contact_information', 'Gender', 'Membership_level', 'Name', 'Points', 'Registration_time'. All these columns allow null values.\n5. **Course_material**: This table holds information about the materials of the courses. The primary key is 'Material_ID', which is an integer. The columns include 'Course_ID', 'Material_URL', and 'Material_name'. The 'Course_ID' column references the 'Course_ID' in the 'Course' table.\n6. **Instructor_teaching**: This table holds information about which instructor teaches which course. The primary key is a composite of 'Instructor_ID' and 'Course_ID'. The 'Course_ID' column references the 'Course_ID' in the 'Course' table, and the 'Instructor_ID' column references the 'Instructor_ID' in the 'Instructor' table.\n7. **Viewing_record**: This table holds information about the viewing records of the chapters by the students. The primary key is a composite of 'Student_ID' and 'Chapter_ID'. The 'Chapter_ID' column references the 'Chapter_ID' in the 'Chapter' table, and the 'Student_ID' column references the 'Student_ID' in the 'Student' table.\nThe schema is designed to maintain the integrity of the data by enforcing primary key and foreign key constraints. It also includes indexes to optimize the performance of the queries.",
  "gold_question": "This is an online education platform's course management system. For course management, the system supports maintaining basic course information (course ID, course name, course description, etc.), records detailed course information (number of lessons, total duration, difficulty level, etc.), and manages course classification information (course category, target audience, recommendation status, etc.). For chapter management, the system maintains basic chapter information (chapter ID, chapter name, chapter description, etc.), records detailed chapter information (video URL, course materials, duration, etc.), and manages chapter sequence (previous/next chapters, chapter hierarchy, etc.). For instructor management, the system maintains basic instructor information (instructor ID, name, avatar, etc.), records detailed instructor information (teaching experience, professional field, personal profile, etc.), and manages instructor courses (teaching list, ratings, student feedback, etc.). For student management, the system maintains basic student information, including basic data (student ID, name, avatar, gender, age, contact information) and account information (registration time, account status, membership level, points), while tracking learning progress, including course progress (selected courses, current learning chapter, last learning time), viewing records (viewing duration per lesson, number of views, completion status) and learning statistics (total learning duration, course completion rate).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0423.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0423\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `course_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `course_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `difficulty_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `number_of_lessons` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recommended` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `target_audience` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_duration` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `chapter` (\n  `chapter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `chapter_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `chapter_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `next_chapter_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `parent_chapter_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `previous_chapter_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `video_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`chapter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `chapter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`next_chapter_id`) REFERENCES `chapter` (`chapter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `chapter_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_chapter_id`) REFERENCES `chapter` (`chapter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `chapter_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`previous_chapter_id`) REFERENCES `chapter` (`chapter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instructor` (\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `professional_field` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `teaching_experience` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`instructor_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `age` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_information` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `membership_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `points` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_material` (\n  `material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `material_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `material_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`material_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_material_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `instructor_teaching` (\n  `instructor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`instructor_id`, `course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `instructor_teaching_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`instructor_id`) REFERENCES `instructor` (`instructor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `instructor_teaching_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `viewing_record` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `chapter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `chapter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `viewing_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `viewing_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`chapter_id`) REFERENCES `chapter` (`chapter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
